# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the webmail origin.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy itself is emitted as a <meta> element by Astro
# (astro.config.mjs `security.csp`), because only the build knows the hashes of
# its own inline hydration scripts. What lives HERE is the set of protections a
# <meta> tag cannot deliver:
#
#   • frame-ancestors is IGNORED in <meta> — the browser says so out loud. It
#     has to be a header, and without it the triage buttons are click-jackable.
#   • HSTS, nosniff and Referrer-Policy are header-only by definition.
#
# Referrer-Policy matters more than usual here: every link in every message is
# attacker-chosen, and a referrer would leak the webmail URL to whoever the
# sender picked.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
